WEBVTT

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.960
Absent-minded, I only prayed to the stars

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:27.760
Losing sight of all that was precious

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.600
Absent-minded, I kept my eyes fixed on the same spot

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:38.310
And came to a standstill myself

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.480
We don't need no reasons

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.570
To change for the better

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:55.870
Now, let's dream to the extreme

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:57.960
You're a shooting star

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.250
Kick open the doors that stand in your way

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.470
And leap beyond the infinite horizon

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.550
Light on the shooting star

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:14.560
Don't look back; what you seek is in front of you

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.680
Let's go in search of it

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.440
Fly away

00:01:40.042 --> 00:01:42.795
I'm hungry…

00:01:42.795 --> 00:01:45.589
Hungry…!

00:01:45.589 --> 00:01:48.634
Hungry!

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:51.470
Hungry…

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.391
M-More! Hit me more!

00:01:55.391 --> 00:01:57.434
What’s going on over there?!

00:02:02.981 --> 00:02:08.612
Urashima went to the Sea God’s Palace,

00:02:08.612 --> 00:02:11.281
taken by the turtle he saved.

00:02:12.199 --> 00:02:14.243
Just like Urashima Tare from the picture book,

00:02:14.243 --> 00:02:19.206
we’ll save that turtle and ask him
to take us to the Sea God’s Palace!

00:02:19.206 --> 00:02:21.250
Give them hell!

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.461
Yes, ma’am!

00:02:24.461 --> 00:02:25.462
You are the…

00:02:25.462 --> 00:02:27.631
They’re Doronjo and her
gang from the wanted list!

00:02:27.631 --> 00:02:28.799
Capture them!

00:02:37.266 --> 00:02:39.226
Let’s go!

00:02:41.854 --> 00:02:44.481
To the Sea God’s Palace!

00:02:44.481 --> 00:02:46.442
You guys are… heavy!

00:02:46.442 --> 00:02:47.693
Hm?

00:02:47.693 --> 00:02:49.778
It’s not a turtle?

00:02:49.778 --> 00:02:53.157
There’s something exciting about
the weight I'm feeling, though…

00:02:53.157 --> 00:02:55.784
ln any case, I'm not a turtle.

00:02:55.784 --> 00:02:58.287
How confusing.

00:02:59.121 --> 00:03:01.623
What’s so confusing?!

00:03:01.623 --> 00:03:04.293
S-Sea God’s Palace…

00:03:12.092 --> 00:03:14.136
At the beach in Tomake?

00:03:14.136 --> 00:03:17.014
Yes, sir! Please take a look
at this, General Goro.

00:03:17.014 --> 00:03:20.476
They were making delirious remarks
about bringing down Lord Yatterman,

00:03:20.476 --> 00:03:25.189
but they’re at the complete opposite side
of Yatter Metropolis. I wonder why…

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:28.317
They’re probably trying to avoid
the checkpoints by making a detour

00:03:28.317 --> 00:03:29.943
to get to the capital city,

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:33.614
but unfortunately, it was a waste of time.

00:03:33.614 --> 00:03:36.658
Sea God’s Palace… What’s that?

00:03:36.658 --> 00:03:39.912
Those are the last words of the
communication with our soldiers.

00:03:39.912 --> 00:03:42.581
Sea God’s Palace, huh?

00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:46.960
There’s an underwater
power plant in Tomake, right?

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.003
Yes, sir.

00:03:48.003 --> 00:03:51.840
We’ll capture Doronjo
and her gang in one swoop!

00:03:54.426 --> 00:03:59.806
Turtle… Sea God’s Palace…
Turtle… Sea God’s Palace…

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:02.351
Thank you for saving me!

00:04:02.351 --> 00:04:07.314
I was chased and got
beaten up by Yatter Soldiers.

00:04:07.314 --> 00:04:11.985
Although it felt a bit good,
I thought I was a goner.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:15.072
You’re being chased by the
Yatter soldiers, too, right?

00:04:15.072 --> 00:04:19.743
I’ve seen you in a wanted poster.
Doronbow, was it?

00:04:21.161 --> 00:04:24.540
You should watch out for that thing.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:29.711
That unmanned drone
Yatter Jonathan is often patrolling.

00:04:29.711 --> 00:04:32.381
By the way, my name is Ryu. I'm a fisherman.

00:04:32.381 --> 00:04:35.842
Fish are good. They make me excited!

00:04:37.052 --> 00:04:39.555
They aren’t listening to me at all.

00:04:40.889 --> 00:04:42.099
That’s…

00:04:44.101 --> 00:04:45.852
You dim-witted turtle!

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:48.480
Stupid turtle! Stupid turtle!

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:52.359
Stop it, turtle. It hurts, turtle.
Stop it, turtle.

00:04:52.359 --> 00:04:56.405
It’s a turtle! A chance to
go to the Sea God’s Palace!

00:04:56.405 --> 00:04:57.823
Hey! Hold on a sec!

00:04:57.823 --> 00:05:02.202
Don’t abuse the turtle!

00:05:02.202 --> 00:05:04.538
Ahh! Get outta here!

00:05:04.538 --> 00:05:06.915
This is clearly fishy.

00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:10.794
Mr. Turtle, are you okay?

00:05:10.794 --> 00:05:12.087
Thank you, turtle.

00:05:12.087 --> 00:05:15.257
As a token of my appreciation, I’ll invite
you all to the Sea God’s Palace, turtle.

00:05:15.257 --> 00:05:17.551
Sea God’s Palace?!

00:05:17.551 --> 00:05:19.469
Now, get in, turtle.

00:05:19.469 --> 00:05:20.929
Sea God’s Palace!

00:05:20.929 --> 00:05:25.100
Hey, you guys, listen to me.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.938
Real turtles are sexier than this, and…

00:05:29.938 --> 00:05:32.858
Huh? A-Already leaving?

00:05:32.858 --> 00:05:34.943
I guess I have no choice.

00:05:43.327 --> 00:05:45.746
See you!

00:05:51.251 --> 00:05:57.132
A long, long time ago, Urashima
went to the Sea God’s Palace,

00:05:57.132 --> 00:05:59.134
taken by the turtle he saved.

00:05:59.134 --> 00:06:02.304
It was such a beautiful place

00:06:02.304 --> 00:06:06.141
but what am I gonna do?
--That a picture wouldn’t do it justice.

00:06:06.141 --> 00:06:08.352
This is clearly a Yatter mecha.

00:06:08.352 --> 00:06:11.146
I wonder what the Sea God’s Palace is like.

00:06:11.146 --> 00:06:14.650
So, a beautiful princess will be waiting for us?

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:16.568
There’ll be a lot of good food!

00:06:16.568 --> 00:06:19.613
Sea breams and flounders will dance for us!

00:06:19.613 --> 00:06:21.990
They’re hopeless…

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.368
They’re like bugs that fly into
the flame on a summer night.

00:06:24.368 --> 00:06:28.121
Or rather, octopuses that swim
into octopus pots in winter.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:31.458
I like how "octopus pot" sounds.

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:35.212
We’ll be arriving at the
Sea God’s Palace shortly, turtle.

00:06:35.212 --> 00:06:37.255
The Sea God’s Palace!

00:06:41.176 --> 00:06:42.636
That’s…

00:06:48.308 --> 00:06:51.853
We’ve arrived at the Sea God’s Palace!

00:06:51.853 --> 00:06:54.106
Welcome to the Palace!

00:06:54.106 --> 00:06:55.857
Princess!

00:06:55.857 --> 00:06:57.609
Sea breams and flounders!

00:06:57.609 --> 00:06:59.403
Is it okay to eat them?

00:07:00.696 --> 00:07:05.033
Thank you very much for saving one
of our precious turtles from bullies.

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:06.785
Where’s the feast?!

00:07:06.785 --> 00:07:11.707
We’ve prepared a lot.
Now, please come this way.

00:07:11.707 --> 00:07:12.791
This room?

00:07:12.791 --> 00:07:14.876
There’s no food here.

00:07:14.876 --> 00:07:19.131
We’re preparing right now.
Before the feast, please take this.

00:07:19.131 --> 00:07:20.674
A treasure box?!

00:07:20.674 --> 00:07:24.010
When you speak of the Sea God’s Palace,
don’t forget the treasure box. Here you go.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:27.305
l see! I wonder what’s inside.

00:07:27.305 --> 00:07:29.599
Miss Doronjo! Please hurry up and open it!

00:07:29.599 --> 00:07:31.268
It’s exciting!

00:07:31.268 --> 00:07:33.311
Exciting, oink!

00:07:33.311 --> 00:07:35.897
It’s better not to open it!

00:07:36.898 --> 00:07:38.150
There!

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:53.457
Okay. Go tell General Goro that we got them.

00:07:53.457 --> 00:07:55.542
Yatterman!

00:07:55.542 --> 00:07:57.502
A piece of cake!

00:07:57.502 --> 00:08:00.255
You’re as amazing as ever, General Goro!

00:08:00.255 --> 00:08:05.302
Now, this’ll allow me to save my honor
in front of Lord Yatterman. Hm?

00:08:11.433 --> 00:08:13.268
Is something wrong?

00:08:13.268 --> 00:08:16.605
No… Have you arranged
the transport vehicle?

00:08:16.605 --> 00:08:21.109
It’s already headed to the Sea God’s Palace…
the underwater power plant.

00:08:21.109 --> 00:08:22.611
Good!

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:29.868
What am I doing?

00:08:29.868 --> 00:08:32.245
The sashimi tastes good!

00:08:32.245 --> 00:08:37.083
I thought I was saved,
but I got caught after all.

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:39.294
I can no longer escape.

00:08:39.294 --> 00:08:43.173
I’ll have some, too, oink!

00:08:43.173 --> 00:08:44.591
Ouch!

00:08:44.591 --> 00:08:45.842
Shh!

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.472
Are you okay?

00:08:50.472 --> 00:08:52.974
Yeah… I think so.

00:08:52.974 --> 00:08:53.975
Where are we?

00:08:53.975 --> 00:08:56.019
You don’t remember anything?

00:08:56.019 --> 00:08:58.980
We’re at the underwater
power plant in Tomake.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.107
Underwater power plant?!

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:05.946
It’s a Yatterman facility that produces
power using the ebb and flow of the tide.

00:09:05.946 --> 00:09:10.992
I see… So we were tricked by
that turtle and brought here…

00:09:10.992 --> 00:09:15.872
I'm good at skin diving, so it’s not hard
for me to hold my breath for a long time.

00:09:15.872 --> 00:09:20.460
When I hold my breath until I can’t
any longer, if feels good, you know.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:23.672
So I didn’t have to breathe that sleeping gas.

00:09:23.672 --> 00:09:26.216
Mr. Ryu, you said you’re a fisherman.

00:09:26.216 --> 00:09:28.718
Why were you in the hands of Yatter Soldiers?

00:09:28.718 --> 00:09:32.931
I was about to be taken away
to do the forced labor, so I ran…

00:09:32.931 --> 00:09:36.643
although the idea of being
slave driven for the rest of my life

00:09:36.643 --> 00:09:39.688
gets me excited in its own way.

00:09:39.688 --> 00:09:42.190
I have a dream.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:43.108
A dream?

00:09:43.108 --> 00:09:46.069
I wanna go to the Sea God’s Palace.

00:09:46.069 --> 00:09:48.822
Sea God’s Palace? There’s no such place…

00:09:48.822 --> 00:09:51.783
I know. I don’t really
believe such a place exists.

00:09:51.783 --> 00:09:56.788
I’ve always loved the creatures
of the sea, such as fish and clams.

00:09:58.164 --> 00:10:01.042
Those smooth scales of fish…

00:10:02.544 --> 00:10:04.838
Those seductive mouths…

00:10:05.881 --> 00:10:09.009
I feel like I want them to
capture me and bind me up.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:13.263
Everything about them is
so perfect. They’re erotic!

00:10:13.263 --> 00:10:15.599
Don’t you agree, Galina?

00:10:15.599 --> 00:10:17.350
Yeah… I guess…

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.687
I learned about the Sea God’s Palace in
the picture book about Urashima Taro.

00:10:20.687 --> 00:10:27.027
A long, long time ago, Urashima went to
a hostess club called Sea God’s Palace,

00:10:27.027 --> 00:10:30.113
taken by the turtle he saved in Susukino.

00:10:30.113 --> 00:10:33.783
a harem with a sumptuous feast.
--I don’t think that’s how the song goes…

00:10:33.783 --> 00:10:38.079
Folk tales have many versions.

00:10:38.079 --> 00:10:40.415
I wanna go to the Sea God’s
Palace of my version.

00:10:40.415 --> 00:10:44.085
I other words, I wanna go
to the other side of the wall.

00:10:44.085 --> 00:10:48.173
I wanna go to the real sea,
not a small one like this.

00:10:48.173 --> 00:10:50.592
I wanna fish in the open sea…

00:10:50.592 --> 00:10:54.888
I wanna capture lots of fish
and feel the infinite Eros!

00:10:54.888 --> 00:10:59.601
That’s the harem for me! But…

00:11:06.107 --> 00:11:10.153
…when I tried to go over the wall,
Yatter Jonathans found me.

00:11:11.112 --> 00:11:13.448
Nooooo!

00:11:16.534 --> 00:11:21.122
I tried to go under water,
but it wasn’t possible.

00:11:23.458 --> 00:11:27.712
Besides those things, I saved
several turtles in trouble, too.

00:11:27.712 --> 00:11:30.632
I even gave them names,
like, Kameko and Kamejiro,

00:11:30.632 --> 00:11:33.468
hoping that they’d return the favor some day…

00:11:33.468 --> 00:11:36.471
that they’d take me to the Sea God’s Palace.

00:11:37.764 --> 00:11:43.061
I wanna go to the real sea… a heavenly harem!

00:11:43.061 --> 00:11:45.814
Heaven… Harem…

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:50.860
But I can’t go to the
Sea God’s Palace anymore…

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:55.824
You can! You can definitely go there… I think.

00:11:55.824 --> 00:11:56.866
Really?

00:11:56.866 --> 00:12:01.663
I have… hope…

00:12:01.663 --> 00:12:03.373
Hope…

00:12:06.568 --> 00:12:09.780
I always thought that I was
going to live like a zombie

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:14.952
in this hellish, dark world of Yatter Kingdom.

00:12:14.952 --> 00:12:16.202
But…

00:12:16.202 --> 00:12:18.246
My angel!

00:12:18.246 --> 00:12:21.166
We’ll bring down Yatterman!

00:12:21.166 --> 00:12:26.380
Ally… Alouette was always crying,
but one day we met Doronjo.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:29.382
She made Ally smile, and now
we travel together with them.

00:12:29.382 --> 00:12:31.468
So I started thinking

00:12:31.468 --> 00:12:35.514
that a light might stream even
into this dark world one day.

00:12:35.514 --> 00:12:36.932
What’s that?

00:12:36.932 --> 00:12:38.434
Just watch.

00:12:38.434 --> 00:12:42.020
Mr. Boyacky teaches me how to
make things, so I made this one myself,

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:44.106
although it’s not finished yet.

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:50.446
I couldn’t do anything before,
but I may be able to change the world.

00:12:50.446 --> 00:12:54.908
If I try, I may be able to do it…
I can think that way now.

00:12:54.908 --> 00:12:56.576
So I won’t give up.

00:12:56.576 --> 00:12:58.704
You are a strong person.

00:12:58.704 --> 00:13:04.752
I-I'm not strong at all. When I wrestle
with Mr. Tonzra, I always lose.

00:13:04.752 --> 00:13:07.378
My. Ryu, what’s your favorite number?

00:13:07.378 --> 00:13:11.300
That’d be two. It’s the number of boobs!

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.802
Then, if we get two, you won’t give up.

00:13:13.802 --> 00:13:15.012
Okay?

00:13:15.012 --> 00:13:16.220
Okay.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.440
--Whoa!
--Boobs!

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:29.734
Okay! You’re right, Galina!

00:13:29.734 --> 00:13:32.112
I won’t give up just yet.

00:13:32.112 --> 00:13:35.574
I'm gonna get out of hell
and head off for a harem!

00:13:35.574 --> 00:13:40.328
"If you give up on your dream,
you’ll see nothing at all in the sea."

00:13:40.328 --> 00:13:41.746
That’s a nice phrase.

00:13:41.746 --> 00:13:45.708
That’s my favorite phrase.
Someone from long ago once said that.

00:13:45.708 --> 00:13:49.004
But what do I do to not give up on it?

00:13:49.004 --> 00:13:50.672
We’ve got our friends.

00:13:50.672 --> 00:13:52.674
First, let’s wake them up.

00:13:52.674 --> 00:13:54.218
Will they wake up?

00:13:56.302 --> 00:13:58.764
Honorable Oda!

00:13:58.764 --> 00:13:59.972
I'm counting on you.

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:10.108
Good morning, little piggy.

00:14:10.108 --> 00:14:11.776
Ouch!

00:14:11.776 --> 00:14:13.654
Miss Doronjo, where are we?

00:14:13.654 --> 00:14:15.656
What on earth happened to us?

00:14:15.656 --> 00:14:18.784
Good! You’re finally back
to your normal selves!

00:14:18.784 --> 00:14:20.368
Normal?

00:14:23.996 --> 00:14:26.750
--If you don’t mind dried sardines, I’ve got some.
--Dried sardines!

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:31.421
Dried sardines are good. Their naughty
looking hips and their hardness…!

00:14:31.421 --> 00:14:33.506
How irresistible!

00:14:35.342 --> 00:14:38.804
Yatterman’s underwater power plant?!

00:14:38.804 --> 00:14:42.974
So, since we were hungry, they took
advantage of it and tricked us?!

00:14:42.974 --> 00:14:45.018
Even though they’re our enemy,
I must say that was brilliant!

00:14:45.018 --> 00:14:46.436
Yeah.

00:14:46.436 --> 00:14:48.772
People normally wouldn’t be
taken in by such an obvious trick.

00:14:48.772 --> 00:14:51.400
We’d better get out of here right away!

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:55.070
What’s with you, Gatchan?
You’re unusually proactive.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:58.740
Anyway, the soldiers I saw earlier
said that they’d carry us out

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.076
once the transport vehicle arrives.

00:15:01.076 --> 00:15:04.580
In any case, we have to escape before that!

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:08.166
So… I came up with a plan.

00:15:08.166 --> 00:15:12.838
Our enemy’s guard is down
because they think we’re sleeping.

00:15:12.838 --> 00:15:14.046
Bring them to the dock!

00:15:14.046 --> 00:15:15.174
Yatter!

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:23.556
So we can easily get out
of this room. And then…

00:15:25.726 --> 00:15:28.520
Take that!

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:31.732
Once we’re at the dock,
Mr. Tonzra will stand watch.

00:15:31.732 --> 00:15:36.986
In the mean time, Mr. Boyacky will take
a Yatturtle apart and build a mecha.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.576
How’re you doing?

00:15:42.576 --> 00:15:47.164
It’ll be done soon.
Boy, you’re a slave driver.

00:15:47.164 --> 00:15:50.208
Did you make that, Gatchan?

00:15:50.208 --> 00:15:53.544
Yes, although it’s not finished yet.

00:15:53.544 --> 00:15:58.424
I see… It’s like a toy.

00:15:58.424 --> 00:16:02.346
A toy… A toy, huh?

00:16:02.346 --> 00:16:05.556
Somehow, Gatchan is…

00:16:05.556 --> 00:16:07.392
Catch them! Don’t let them get away!

00:16:07.392 --> 00:16:09.018
Yatterman!

00:16:09.018 --> 00:16:10.646
Boyacky!

00:16:10.646 --> 00:16:13.898
Yes, ma’am! It’s done!

00:16:15.108 --> 00:16:17.818
Since they kicked our butts,
we’ll kick them right back!

00:16:17.818 --> 00:16:19.738
And, open!

00:16:22.032 --> 00:16:24.284
How impudent!

00:16:27.162 --> 00:16:29.414
Octopus!

00:16:42.802 --> 00:16:44.304
Stop right there!

00:16:47.224 --> 00:16:49.308
Octopus!

00:17:02.406 --> 00:17:04.116
All right!

00:17:09.037 --> 00:17:10.622
Wrong one!

00:17:13.625 --> 00:17:15.085
Is this good, this spot, oink?

00:17:15.085 --> 00:17:16.962
A bit more to the right, oink.

00:17:16.962 --> 00:17:19.714
This spot? Is it better here, oink?

00:17:19.714 --> 00:17:21.675
Ah, yes, right there, oink.

00:17:21.675 --> 00:17:23.676
It worked!

00:17:23.676 --> 00:17:27.180
You nerdles! Hurdles! Turdles! Turtles!

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:30.600
The octopus was just a decoy.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:33.520
They didn’t seem to notice that
the one they really should go after was

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:36.315
this "ls-This-Spot-Good Giant Squid".

00:17:36.315 --> 00:17:40.902
In any case… you’ve got good taste in names.

00:17:40.902 --> 00:17:44.780
Gatchan’s right. Those in power are
always looking above themselves

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.200
and not watching their own feet.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.994
That was a good plan, Gatchan!

00:17:51.121 --> 00:17:56.585
I had faith that you guys
would make it all work, so…

00:17:59.838 --> 00:18:03.216
O-Okay. We’ll keep going like this
to break the power generator fans

00:18:03.216 --> 00:18:04.968
and go to the other side!

00:18:04.968 --> 00:18:07.054
Yes, ma’am!

00:18:08.305 --> 00:18:10.682
We can now see the fans!

00:18:10.682 --> 00:18:13.268
Get the foot missiles ready!

00:18:15.186 --> 00:18:17.189
Fire!

00:18:20.901 --> 00:18:22.568
What’s going on?!

00:18:22.568 --> 00:18:24.738
Miss Doronjo, look!

00:18:24.738 --> 00:18:26.114
What’s that?

00:18:26.114 --> 00:18:27.406
An anglerfish?

00:18:27.406 --> 00:18:29.868
No, I don’t think so. That’s…

00:18:29.868 --> 00:18:32.954
An ocean sunfish! It’s Yattersunfish!

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:38.042
The transport vehicle arrived in time!

00:18:38.042 --> 00:18:43.882
I’ll cram you in this Yattersunfish
and send you to General Goro!

00:18:46.634 --> 00:18:48.595
Hurry up and fire!

00:18:48.595 --> 00:18:52.891
It’s not working! That shock made
it unable to release the feet!

00:18:52.891 --> 00:18:55.018
We can’t fire the missiles!

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:07.406
Gatchan, what should we do?

00:19:07.406 --> 00:19:08.240
What do we do?

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:11.326
You should’ve thought of backup plans!

00:19:11.326 --> 00:19:15.580
Like, if Plan A doesn’t work, then Plan B!
If that doesn’t work either, then Plan C!

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:20.919
You’ve got more to learn!
Now that it’s come to this…

00:19:20.919 --> 00:19:22.378
What’re we gonna do?

00:19:22.378 --> 00:19:27.008
We’ll stop one of the fans, so use
that chance and go to the other side!

00:19:27.008 --> 00:19:28.926
You’re good at skin diving, right?!

00:19:28.926 --> 00:19:30.971
B-But…

00:19:30.971 --> 00:19:32.972
Mr. Ryu! Go!

00:19:32.972 --> 00:19:35.850
You have to go! To achieve your dream!

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:38.103
And we have to go, too!

00:19:39.229 --> 00:19:40.355
Thank you!

00:19:40.355 --> 00:19:42.482
Boyacky! Tonzra!

00:19:42.482 --> 00:19:44.568
Yes, ma’am!

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:49.906
What’re they trying to do?!

00:19:49.906 --> 00:19:51.575
Now!

00:19:51.575 --> 00:19:54.411
That’s the tentacle play that I dreamed of!

00:19:57.788 --> 00:19:59.290
Stop it!

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:08.340
Hurry!

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:10.093
Mr. Ryu!

00:20:30.822 --> 00:20:32.406
This won’t last much longer!

00:20:32.406 --> 00:20:35.035
This isn’t good!

00:20:35.035 --> 00:20:36.494
Mr. Ryu!

00:20:37.746 --> 00:20:42.000
I can’t do it… After all, I…

00:20:43.418 --> 00:20:49.298
No, I won’t give up!
Never! I promised Galina!

00:20:50.926 --> 00:20:57.182
Kameko?! Kamejiro?! Kameta?!
Kamekichi?! Kamebou?! Kamemi?!

00:20:58.683 --> 00:21:02.854
Your bodies have gotten sexy!

00:21:12.113 --> 00:21:14.990
Thank you, guys!

00:21:33.884 --> 00:21:37.096
He did it… He did it!

00:21:37.096 --> 00:21:42.394
Yeah… Ryu went… to the Sea God’s Palace.

00:21:42.394 --> 00:21:46.231
Now, we’re gonna head out,
too, to Yatter Metropolis!

00:21:46.231 --> 00:21:48.650
We have to try hard, just like Ryu did!

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:51.570
We’ll bring down Yatterman at any cost!

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:53.488
Ah-choo!

00:21:55.282 --> 00:22:00.120
So, this is… the real… sea?!

00:22:01.954 --> 00:22:07.252
Now I'm going… to my harem!

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:18.090
Should I raise my RPM and dream?

00:22:20.300 --> 00:22:25.720
Don't put it off for tomorrow, do it now

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:28.020
My strong heart wants to get started

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:30.100
I want to see change, so let's go

00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:35.650
I'm running too fast to smell the roses

00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:37.690
My strong heart's at max speed

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:40.280
I made a wish because I wanted a change

00:22:40.280 --> 00:22:44.240
I search, I tire, I fall, and I get back up

00:22:44.240 --> 00:22:50.870
I'll enjoy this every time

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:53.540
Continue your passion

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:56.000
Continue your passion

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:57.290
I'll support you

00:22:57.290 --> 00:22:58.250
I'm on your side

00:22:58.250 --> 00:22:59.510
Jump, jump, pushing the limits is my life story

00:22:59.510 --> 00:23:01.300
Jump, jump, pushing the limits is my life story

00:23:01.300 --> 00:23:05.760
My drive ain't no work of fiction

00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:06.970
I want to see you

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:08.010
Today, if I can

00:23:08.010 --> 00:23:09.770
After all, my fingers just won't stop

00:23:09.770 --> 00:23:11.140
After all, my fingers just won't stop

00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:15.230
Don't you know?

00:23:12.980 --> 00:23:16.560
Day and night, I'm missing you

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:17.900
The world might get you down,

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:17.900
Nothing in the world is going your way

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.820
The world might get you down,

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:20.280
Nothing in the world is going your way

00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:23.030
But continue your passions

00:23:23.030 --> 00:23:26.200
But continue your passions

00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:38.000
Keep praying and dreaming
